index c507d1c..12d339c 100644
--- a/docs/bots.md
+++ b/docs/bots.md
@@ -27,6 +27,19 @@ open rooms by default — see [Room membership](#room-membership).
 - Pages send `Cache-Control: no-store` since they show credentials. No pagination.
 - Form params use the `user` key (`form_with model: @bot`).
 
+### Bot limit ("Bots per member")
+
+- `Account#bots_per_member` (`settings.bots_per_member`, `has_json` default `5`, validated as an
+  integer >= 0). Set by administrators in a number field on `/account/edit` that submits on change;
+  invalid values redirect back with an alert instead of raising.
+- `User#reached_bot_limit?` – `false` for administrators; otherwise compares `bots.active.count`
+  (deleted/deactivated bots don't count) with the limit. `User#bot_limit` reads it from `Current.account`.
+- Enforced in the model: `User::Bot` validates `creator_within_bot_limit` **on create**, so every
+  creation path (`BotsController#create`, `User.create_bot!`, consoles) is refused. Being an
+  on-create check, lowering the limit never touches existing bots — it only blocks new ones.
+- UI: at the limit, `bots/index` replaces "Add a chat bot" with a "You've reached the limit…" note,
+  and `BotsController#new` redirects to `/bots` with an alert.
+
